6,"Culture of Nepal - history, people, clothing, traditions, women, beliefs...",https://www.everyculture.com/Ma-Ni/Nepal.html,"Nepali culture represents a fusion of Indo-Aryan and Tibeto-Mongolian influences, the result of a long history of migration, conquest, and trade. Location and Geography. Nepal is a roughly rectangular country with an area of 147,181 square miles (381,200 square kilometers).",Nepali,Indo-European
7,"Culture and Traditions of Nepal - Customs, Etiquette, & Language",https://www.travelogyindia.com/nepal/culture-and-traditions-of-nepal.html,Indo-Nepalese mostly migrated from different parts of India. This group follows Hinduism and speaks Nepali with a mix of Indo-Aryan languages. They are more common in the Terai region. The Tibeto-Nepalese migrated from Tibet and speak Nepali with a mix of Tibeto-Burmese.,Nepali,Indo-European
